  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: PCA (pca_n2000) with singleprofile RNA is the best configuration so far (acc 0.485), outperforming scgpt RNA (0.411) and image-only ResNet50 (0.208). The image modality appears weak, and scgpt underperforms PCA. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested whether multiprofile aggregation (using multiple views/profiles per cell) can improve on the singleprofile baseline for the best-performing encoder. This experiment (config_002: rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) isolates the effect of profile setting while holding the RNA encoder fixed at the best-performing PCA. Avgpool is chosen as the simpler aggregation to first establish whether multiprofile helps at all before testing the more complex transformer. This is the best use of experiment 4 because it directly extends the strongest result with a single, interpretable design change, and the answer will guide whether to invest remaining budget in multiprofile variants (including multimodal multiprofile) or pivot to other directions like alternative encoders or multimodal fusion."
}

